[debug] [2026-11-12T07:31:32.735Z] <<< [apiv2][body] POST https://firebaserules.googleapis.com/v1/projects/widebed-pmsdashboard/rulesets {"name":"projects/widebed-pmsdashboard/rulesets/3ed1505b-e1d1-4f60-96df-08a9f16a8d12","source":{"files":[{"content":"rules_version = '2';\n// Widebed PMS Firestore rules. Draft 0.61, 12 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance, several locations. config/attendance may hold\n// `places` (up to 30: name, address, lat, lng, radiusM, cosLat), the company's properties next to the main office. A clock-in /\n// clock-out inside one is Normal and saves which one (clockInPlaceIdx / clockOutPlaceIdx: -1 = the main office, else the\n// place's position in the list) and its name (clockInPlace / clockOutPlace, 'WIDEBED' for the main office); the server checks\n// the phone really is inside the place it names. Outside all of them it is Off-site (if allowed) and the place text is the\n// address the phone looked up (up to 200 characters). Apps from before this draft still work (main office only). Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.60, 12 Nov 2026 (Khairul): sharedRates = one set of fees and rates for every\n// property (Portfolio > Fees & Rates). Read and add-only create, the same people as a property's rateVersions. Nothing else changed.\n// Draft 0.59, 12 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance, holidays per person. A public holiday\n// (attendanceHolidays/{date}) may leave some staff out (exceptUids: a list of uids, HR unticks them in the PMS). For them that\n// date is a normal working day: clocking in is not an Off day and late counts. Holidays now accept only name, exceptUids\n// (up to 300), addedBy/addedAt and updatedBy/updatedAt. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.58, 12 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Operations read owners/{id}/private/main, so Portfolio\n// shows them owner names (Marketing already could). The page shows only the name; nothing else changed.\n// Draft 0.57, 12 Nov 2026 (Khairul, state security Phase 2): records carry their property's\n// `state` (owners, tenants and eZee uploads a `states` list). The lists of allowed keys take state/states, a Director\n// may change only state/states on any property-linked record (Stamp states tool, stampOnly()), and Operations may refresh\n// an owner's `states`. Nothing is locked by state yet (that is Phase 4); no other check changed.\n// Draft 0.56, 12 Nov 2026 (Khairul, state security Phase 1): a new property may carry a\n// top-level `state` (Operations' add-property check listed every allowed key and refused it). Nothing else changed;\n// the state lock itself comes in a later draft.\n// Draft 0.55, 11 Nov 2026 (Khairul): republish only. Neo's Draft 0.54 (attendance off-site) with\n// Khairul's Draft 0.53 (Owner Leads statuses) kept, so neither drops the other. No rule changes.\n// Draft 0.54, 11 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance off-site. Staff may clock in and out away from the office;\n// each clock-in / clock-out is saved with InArea true (Normal) or false (Off-site), and the server checks that flag against its own\n// distance sum, so it can't be faked as Normal. HR / Directors can turn off-site off in config/attendance (allowOffsite: false):\n// then, as before, only inside the office area. Fake-GPS is still refused. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.53, 11 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Owner Leads statuses. newOwnerListings status may be\n// inProgress (older), progress, signed, live or cancelled (Not proceeding). Status and its fields (prevStatus, signedAt,\n// liveAt, cancelledAt/By/ByUid, cancelReason) change only by Directors and Procurement (also from the TMS, which writes as\n// the signed-in person); Marketing may only take a listing to Live (with liveAt). Only Directors reopen a cancelled one.\n// The owner's phone and email (newOwnerListings/{id}/private/main) now only Directors and Procurement read and write.\n// Draft 0.52, 11 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance, several clock-ins a day. After clocking out, staff can clock in\n// again (out to a client and back): session 2, 3… up to 10 (attendance/{uid}_{day}_s2 …), only once the one before is clocked out,\n// still inside the office area with the server's time; late is decided only by the day's first clock-in. HR / Director\n// corrections may also fix a later session. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.51, 11 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance corrections. On the PMS Attendance page (HR > Attendance) HR and\n// Directors can add a missing day or fix a clock-in / clock-out for anyone except themselves, with a note (editNote) and their\n// uid and the server time (editedBy, editedAt). The record's person and date never change. Still nobody deletes. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.50, 11 Nov 2026 (Khairul): anonymous senders can reply in their staff complaint's\n// conversation (and add photos or documents) while it isn't Closed; nothing naming them is saved (no byUid, no byName).\n// Documents on Director complaints too (HR's Drive; the Directors and the HR sender). docs may carry threadId (a chat photo).\n// Draft 0.49 (Neo), 11 Nov 2026: Staff Attendance (Flutter app on this same Firebase project, PMS sign-in).\n// attendance/{uid}_{YYYY-MM-DD}: one record per person per Malaysia day. Any active staff member creates only their own,\n// for today, with the server's time, inside the office area (config/attendance: lat, lng, radiusM, cosLat, lateAfterMin,\n// workDays). After lateAfterMin (9:10 AM) on a working day the record must say late with a typed reason; on a weekend or a\n// holiday (attendanceHolidays/{date}) it is offDay. Clock out once, the same day, inside the area, then workedMinutes once\n// (checked against the two server times); nothing else can change.\n// Staff read only their own; HR and Directors read all. Nobody deletes. attendanceHolidays: everyone reads, HR and Directors\n// write. config/attendance: everyone reads (config/{docId} allows only some roles), HR and Directors write. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.48, 11 Nov 2026 (Khairul): documents on staff complaints (complaints/{id}/docs: name and\n// Drive file id; the files sit in HR's own Google Drive). Read by the same people as the conversation. Added by HR, by the\n// named sender while it isn't Closed, or by an anonymous sender only in the first 15 minutes (no uid). Never changed or removed.\n// Draft 0.47, 10 Nov 2026: Issues <-> TMS Maintenance link. Directors and the tagged roles can\n// change a ticket's title, description and property (its card is on that property's board in the TMS), and its tmsStatus (the task system column the ticket's card is in, a map\n// { name, for }), with or without a status change, while it is Open or In progress. The task system (TMS) writes these as\n// the signed-in person, with their own PMS sign-in, so the same people can change the same tickets. Mark completed through\n// this rule also needs doneByUid == the person. Nothing else changes; Completed tickets stay locked.\n// Draft 0.46, 6 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Pool Sharing check on Month-end: Accounting / Directors save\n// \"Confirmed 0 bookings\" on a month document (poolZero only). Month summaries (unitMonths) may hold\n// 'arrangementType'. Fee arrangements need no change: they are saved on the property's rateVersions, which Accounting /\n// Directors already create.\n// Draft 0.45, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR can make a salary advance form for a staff member\n// (advances byHR: created straight at Reviewed, within 50% of their salary, not interns, never for themselves), with the form\n// and the signature-use line in the same save. The staff member reads it but can't sign it in the PMS (paper only; HR marks it\n// signed outside). Also (6 Nov 2026): the Procurement Forms page is removed, so procurementForms.view leaves the procurement preset.\n// Also (6 Nov 2026): SOPs get an icon (a short icon name HR picks).\n// Also (6 Nov 2026): HR and Directors can delete an SOP: a soft delete (deleted: true with a reason), the record stays.\n// Also (6 Nov 2026): HR can make new SOPs (sops/{key}: any lower-case key with dashes, with a title and short line), not only the first four.\n// Also (6 Nov 2026): issues get a type (customer or inhouse); Directors and the tagged roles can change it while the ticket is open or in progress.\n// Draft 0.44, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): salary advance requests no longer need a \"needed by\" date\n// (the field is optional; older requests keep theirs). Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.43, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): salary advance review no longer asks how the Director was\n// told (the tick alone, saved with HR's name and time). Only the chloeTold.how check is removed. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.42, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Salary advances (0.41 was never published; this replaces it).\n// staffHR/{uid} (IC, position, salary) and advanceLimits/{uid} (50% of salary, same save): HR and Directors write; HR can't\n// change their own. The person reads only their own limit. Interns (users/{uid}.intern) can't ask for an advance.\n// advances/{id}: staff create their own (Submitted, amount <= 50% of the salary in staffHR), read their own, withdraw while\n// Submitted, and sign once Reviewed (signed/main, drawn or uploaded). HR (never on their own request): Review (amount, Director\n// told; frozen form advances/{id}/form/main + signatureUses/{id} in the same batch), mark signed outside the PMS (fully signed\n// document signed/copy required), add or replace signed/copy later, Approve (pending payment), Paid (payment type, date,\n// screenshot payment/main), Reject at Submitted or Signed. form and signed: the staff member, HR and Directors read; payment:\n// HR and Directors only. advances/{id}/notes: HR writes, HR and Directors read. signatures/director: HR and Directors.\n// counters/advances for SA- refs. Nothing is deleted. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.40, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): second fix for 0.38. HR still couldn't read the private\n// part (subject, details) of their own Director complaint. dirSide() now reads the complaint and the role once each, the\n// private-part rule is split into separate lines, and a backup line lets HR read a private part whose fromUid is theirs.\n// Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.39, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): fix for 0.38. HR's \"my Director complaints\" list\n// (kind == director, fromId == me) was refused because the read rule used get('fromId', null), which a list query can't\n// be checked against. It now compares resource.data.fromId directly. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.38, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Director complaints are private to the HR person who sent\n// them. A new Director complaint keeps the sender's uid (fromId) on the main record; HR reads only their own Director\n// complaints (record, private part, conversation, photos) and replies only on those. Directors still read all. Staff\n// complaints unchanged (HR reads all). Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.37, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR Announcements. announcements/{id}: anyone signed in reads\n// the ones meant for their role or Everyone; HR and Directors read all, post, edit and delete. announcements/{id}/views/{uid}:\n// written once by that person (first time they open it), read by that person, HR and Directors. announcementReads/{uid}: the\n// person's own list of opened announcements, only they read and write it. Files go to Google Drive, not Firestore. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.36, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): delete a cancelled offline booking for good. Accounting,\n// Directors and Operations may delete an offlineBookings document whose status is 'cancelled', with its private part and\n// its utility bill (utilityBills/{same id}). Cancelling itself needed no change. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.35, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.34 below): joint owners. An owner's\n// private part may hold coOwners (extra owners' names and contact details), so Operations (adding an owner) and Marketing\n// (editing names and contact details) may write it too. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.34, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo, on top of Khairul's Draft 0.33 below): COH questions added\n// mid-quarter. An evaluator who already submitted (even if HR/Director approved it) can add answers to the new\n// questions; the evaluation goes back to 'submitted' for review. Once approved, the scores document can only grow\n// (earlier answers can't be removed). Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.33, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.32 below): puts back Khairul's\n// Draft 0.30 and 0.31, which were missing from 0.32: the Directors set a Director complaint's status (Read by the Directors /\n// In review / Closed, closing note in the conversation, HR can't reply once Closed), the Directors' own notes\n// (complaints/{id}/notes on a 'director' complaint, Directors only), and the sender's uid (fromUid) on a complaint's\n// private part for the profile picture. Also fixes the What's New rule (updates/{id}), whose first line had been cut\n// to the top of the file. Nothing else changes.\n// Draft 0.32, 4 Nov 2026: every staff member can do COH and KPI self-rating.\n// (1) cohEvaluations/{id}/private/scores: read/create/update no longer call get() on a parent that may not exist\n// yet (first \"Evaluate\" probe, and the batch that creates the evaluation + its scores together). get() on a missing\n// document errors, and an error means deny, so only roles with another way in (Director, HR, Finance via the\n// private catch-all) could evaluate. Create now uses existsAfter/getAfter; read allows the not-found probe.\n// (2) The private catch-all no longer covers cohEvaluations, so Finance can't read other people's COH marks.\n// (3) kpiConversations / kpiDiscussions reads get the same (resource == null && anyStaff()) probe guard.\n// Draft 0.31, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo): KPI Director Review workflow—\n// kpiSubmissions enhanced with director review fields (directorRating, directorComments, discussionStatus,\n// discussionHistory, discussionThreadId). Employee can resubmit/discuss while director can send back,\n// re-rate, or approve. Discussion threads in kpiDiscussions/{id} allow back-and-forth before final approval.\n// Draft 0.30, 4 Nov 2026 (merge): Khairul's Draft 0.29 (Director complaint\n// threads/photos) rebased onto a snapshot that predated six read-rule fixes from earlier the same day — those\n// are reapplied here. The bug: cohEvaluations/kpiAssignments/kpiSubmissions/performanceDiscussions/\n// performanceTmsSnapshots/performanceResults all checked resource.data.<field> without first handling\n// resource == null. Firestore errors out evaluating .data on a null resource (i.e. the document doesn't exist\n// yet), and a rule error means deny — so any getDoc() probing \"does this exist yet\" (a brand-new KPI task, an\n// evaluation that hasn't happened yet, etc.) got permission-denied instead of a normal \"not found.\" Each of\n// the six now starts with (resource == null && anyStaff()) || so that probe is allowed through safely; no\n// other access was widened. PULL BEFORE EDITING, same as always — this file is edited by both Khairul and Neo.\n// Draft 0.29, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Director complaints (HR to the Directors) get the same\n// conversation and photos: HR and Directors read and write complaints/{id}/thread and /images of a 'director' complaint.\n// Draft 0.28, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.26 below): staff complaint follow-up\n// and photos put back (they were Khairul's 0.26 / 0.27 and missing from Neo's copy): HR sets Read by HR / In review / Closed;\n// complaints/{id}/thread (HR and the NAMED sender write, the sender reads); complaints/{id}/notes (HR only);\n// complaints/{id}/images (one shrunk photo each, read like the conversation). Nothing in them is ever edited or deleted.\n// PULL BEFORE EDITING: this file is edited by both Khairul and Neo, and the last publish wins.\n// Draft 0.26, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo): COH evaluation marks are no longer on the evaluatee-readable\n// cohEvaluations document — they live in a private/scores sub-document only the evaluator and HR/Director can read,\n// so the person being rated never sees the exact score a specific colleague gave them (evaluator identity stays\n// visible, by the existing confirmed business rule).\n// Draft 0.25, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR opening a New staff complaint marks it Read by HR (status 'read').\n// Draft 0.24, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.23 below): push notifications\n// (pushTokens/{token}, one per device, written and read only by the person signed in there; api/push.js reads them with the\n// service account) and Finance/Director may permanently delete a booking that was removed by hand on Month-end.\n// Draft 0.23, 3 Nov 2026 (Neo): Performance Management Stage 1 + Stage 2 (audit\n// remediation): performanceQuarters update is split into a draft-only full-edit branch, a status-only\n// lifecycle-advance branch, and a Director-only finalized->pendingApproval reopen branch, so a quarter's\n// config can't be changed once it leaves draft. performanceResults no longer has an unconditional Director\n// bypass alongside the finalized check (the two branches were OR'd, so the bypass made the check meaningless);\n// there is now exactly one non-finalized write condition, plus one deliberate, revision-tracked correction\n// path (Director only, straight from 'finalized', revisionNumber+1, reason + corrector required) paired with\n// an immutable performanceResults/{id}/revisions/{rev} snapshot of the pre-correction values. kpiSubmissions'\n// employee branch no longer accepts a write once the submission is already approved or rejected, so an\n// employee can't reset a reviewed submission back to 'submitted' to erase the reviewer's decision. (This\n// reapplies Draft \"Stage 1\" fixes that were dropped when this file was rebased from an older snapshot while\n// Draft 0.21/0.22 notification work landed — see PERFORMANCE_MANAGEMENT_HANDOFF.md.)\n// Draft 0.22, 3 Nov 2026: Notifications page clean-up: the recipient may delete a notification\n// sent to them personally, and hide a team (role) notification for themselves only (hiddenBy).\n// Draft 0.21, 3 Nov 2026 (Khairul + Neo combined): Neo's merge (below) plus Khairul's\n// Draft 0.21: notifications may go to roles made on the Roles page (roles/{id} exists), not only the 7 built-in roles.\n// Neo's merge, 3 Nov 2026: base Draft 0.20, with two fixes restored from the stale root firestore.rules (agreement\n// renewals staff-read on users/{uid}, agreementLinks delete support), PLUS the new Performance Management collections.\n// firebase.json deploys THIS file (firebase/firestore.rules). The root firestore.rules is stale and not deployed.\n//\n// Draft 0.20, 3 Nov 2026: ticket quotes and invoices (issueQuotes/{ticketId}: anyone on the ticket adds and reads\n// the quote, Director and Expenses Edit approve and add it to the owner's unit expenses). Draft 0.19, 3 Nov 2026:\n// What's New page (updates/{id}: every staff member reads, Director posts, edits, deletes). Draft 0.18, 3 Nov 2026:\n// owner payment status on statements (Pending Payment / Paid, Invoices & Receipts), no reopen once Paid, Director\n// can delete an unused custom role. Draft 0.18, 2 Nov 2026 (restored from root firestore.rules): agreement renewals\n// — every staff member may read the staff list (names for the \"In charge\" picker on agreements).\n// Draft 0.17, 2 Nov 2026: roles/{id} (Roles page: new roles and changed usual pages, Director only), myPerms reads\n// them. Draft 0.17, 30 Oct 2026 (restored from root firestore.rules): fill-in links can be deleted (agreementLinks).\n// Draft 0.16, 30 Oct 2026: Neo's Draft 0.15 (agreement master files, fill-in links, 'submitted' record status) plus\n// booking numbers (lodgmentCounters), the Willow booking import into offlineBookings,\n// and Operations editing booking details (reservationLodgments rules removed).\n// Offline payments: Operations may view the page (preset) and fill in a payment with status Unknown, which becomes Edited; an Offline Payments View tick no longer opens the other finance data.\n// Draft 0.14, 30 Oct 2026: Draft 0.13 plus Agreements (forms, templates, records, views,\n// generated PDFs). Every staff member fills in agreement forms and reads every record. Forms and templates change only with\n// the \"Agreement Setup\" tick (Directors always). Files (PDFs, IC copies) are in Google Drive, not Firestore.\n// Draft 0.13, 29 Oct 2026: Draft 0.12 (page access, Neo) plus utilityBills and booking door passcodes.\n// users/{uid}.perms (ticked on Staff accounts) lists the pages a person may view or edit: '<page>.view' / '<page>.edit'.\n// No perms saved = the role's preset (presetFor below), so accounts that were never changed behave as in Draft 0.10.\n// Data is protected per area: any Finance page opens the finance data, Portfolio Edit opens owners/units/terms, and so on.\n// Directors keep everything. Statement approvals, Director Override, brand logos, staff accounts, the audit log and\n// complaints still follow the role only and can't be ticked.\n// Draft 0.10, 27 Oct 2026: (1) notifications: an anonymous complaint alert to HR may be created with no sender (createdByUid null);\n// (2) complaints: staff complaints are readable by HR only (Directors keep Director complaints).\n// 27 Oct (Khairul): Marketing may add and edit properties, units and owners (no money/bank) and edit New Owner Listings.\n// History: 0.34 COH new questions after submitting. 0.33 Director complaint status/notes, fromUid, What's New fix.\n// 0.32 COH/KPI for every staff member (null-safe scores rules, Finance no longer reads COH marks).\n// 0.30 six resource==null read-rule fixes reapplied. 0.29 Director complaint threads/photos. 0.28 staff\n// complaint thread/photos/notes. 0.26 COH marks moved to a private sub-document (evaluatee can't read scores).\n// 0.25 HR complaint read-marking.\n// 0.24 push notifications; Finance/Director delete a hand-removed booking. 0.23 Performance Management Stage 1+2\n// (security fixes, revision workflow). 0.22 clear notifications (delete own, hide team ones). 0.21 notifications to\n// custom roles; Performance Management collections (Neo's merge). 0.20 ticket quotes & invoices. 0.19 What's New.\n// 0.18 agreement renewals (staff list readable); owner payment status, custom role delete. 0.17 delete fill-in\n// links; Roles page. 0.16 booking numbers, Willow booking import, Operations edit bookings, offline payments for\n// Operations. 0.15 master files, fill-in links (Neo). 0.14 Agreements. 0.13 utility bills, door passcodes, offline\n// payments, unit types. 0.12 page access. 0.10 anonymous complaint notifications. 0.9 New Owner Listings.\n// 0.8 profile pictures (avatars). 0.7 month summaries (unitMonths, months.summary).\n// 0.6 every role signs in; Portfolio for Operations/Procurement/Marketing; direct bookings. 0.5 offline inquiries,\n// tenants, offline bookings, Issues, SOPs, complaints, Playbook, brand logos. 0.4 month-end completion is per unit.\n// 0.3 HR manages staff accounts and reads the audit log.\n// Merged in: rules_ops.txt, rules_dash.txt, rules_directbooking.txt, rules_hr.txt, rules_portfolio.txt, rules_scale.txt.\n// Roles come from users/{uid}.role, set on the Staff accounts page (or tools/set-role.js for the first Director).\n// Rules OR together: a request is allowed if any matching allow line allows it.\nservice cloud.firestore {\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\n\n    // ================= Helpers =================\n\n    // ---- Roles ----\n    function signedIn()   { return request.auth != null; }\n    // The role is read from the person's staff record. A switched-off record (active == false) has no role.\n    function myRecord()   { return /databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid); }\n    function role() {\n      return signedIn() && exists(myRecord()) && get(myRecord()).data.get('active', true) == true\n        ? get(myRecord()).data.get('role', null) : null;\n    }\n    function isDirector() { return role() == 'director'; }\n    function isIT()       { return role() == 'it'; }\n    function isHR()       { return role() == 'hr'; }\n    function opsRole()    { return role() == 'operations'; }\n    // Any active staff record with a role (every role, including IT).\n    function anyStaff()   { return role() != null; }\n    // Staff accounts: Director and HR. HR can't create, edit or promote anyone to Director.\n    function staffAdmin() { return isDirector() || isHR(); }\n    function hrOrDir()    { return isHR() || isDirector(); }\n\n    // ---- Page access (Draft 0.12) ----\n    // What each role gets before anyone changes its ticks. KEEP IN STEP WITH PRESETS in lib/access.js.\n    function presetFor(r) {\n      return {\n        'finance': ['reports.view', 'reports.edit', 'ezeeUpload.view', 'ezeeUpload.edit', 'expenses.view', 'expenses.edit',\n          'monthEnd.view', 'monthEnd.edit', 'invoices.view', 'invoices.edit', 'offlinePayments.view', 'offlinePayments.edit',\n          'portfolio.view', 'portfolio.edit', 'bulkUpload.view', 'bulkUpload.edit', 'offlineInquiries.view', 'offlineInquiries.edit'],\n        'operations': ['portfolio.view', 'offlineInquiries.view', 'offlineInquiries.edit', 'bookingForms.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'offlinePayments.view'],\n        'it': [],\n        'hr': ['playbook.edit', 'sops.edit'],\n        'procurement': ['portfolio.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'newOwnerListings.edit'],\n        'marketing': ['portfolio.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'newOwnerListings.edit']\n      }.get(r, []);\n    }\n    // Draft 0.17: the Director can change a role's usual pages and make new roles on the Roles page, saved in roles/{id}.\n    // A role with a roles/{id} document uses its perms list; the built-in lists above are the fallback.\n    function roleDoc(r)     { return /databases/$(database)/documents/roles/$(r); }\n    function roleDefault(r) { return exists(roleDoc(r)) ? get(roleDoc(r)).data.get('perms', presetFor(r)) : presetFor(r); }\n    // The person's ticks: saved on their record, or their role's usual pages. A switched-off record has none.\n    function myPerms()    { return role() != null ? get(myRecord()).data.get('perms', roleDefault(role())) : []; }\n    function can(p)       { return isDirector() || p in myPerms(); }\n\n    // Finance data: any Finance page lets them read it; any Finance page ticked for Edit lets them change it.\n    function finEdit()    { return isDirector() || myPerms().hasAny(['ezeeUpload.edit', 'expenses.edit', 'monthEnd.edit', 'invoices.edit', 'offlinePayments.edit']); }\n    function finView()    { return finEdit() || myPerms().hasAny(['reports.view', 'ezeeUpload.view', 'expenses.view', 'monthEnd.view', 'invoices.view']); }\n    function finOrDir()   { return finEdit(); }\n    function isFinance()  { return finEdit(); }\n    // Finance-data readers, plus IT (view-only on everything, as before).\n    function staff()      { return finView() || isIT(); }\n    // Offline Inquiries page: works the inquiries assigned to them (Create booking, tenants, direct bookings).\n    function isOps()      { return can('offlineInquiries.view'); }\n    // Portfolio: View reads owners, properties, units and bookings. Edit (or Bulk Upload Edit) changes them,\n    // terms and bank details included.\n    function portfolioViewer() { return can('portfolio.view'); }\n    function portfolioEditor() { return finEdit() || can('portfolio.edit') || can('bulkUpload.edit'); }\n    // Operations and Marketing with Portfolio View may also add properties, units and owners (no terms or bank details).\n    function portfolioAdder()  { return role() in ['operations', 'marketing'] && portfolioViewer(); }\n    // Marketing with Portfolio View also edit names and details (Khairul 27 Oct).\n    function isMkt()      { return role() == 'marketing' && portfolioViewer(); }\n    // New Owner Listings.\n    function listingViewer()   { return can('newOwnerListings.view'); }\n    function listingEditor()   { return can('newOwnerListings.edit'); }\n    // Draft 0.51: lead statuses\n    function listingMover()    { return isDirector() || role() == 'procurement'; }\n    function listingStatuses() { return ['inProgress', 'progress', 'signed', 'live', 'cancelled']; }\n    function oldListingStatus() { return resource.data.get('status', 'inProgress'); }\n    function listingStatusOk() {\n      return !changed().hasAny(['status', 'prevStatus', 'signedAt', 'liveAt', 'cancelledAt', 'cancelledBy', 'cancelledByUid', 'cancelReason'])\n        || (listingMover() && (isDirector() || oldListingStatus() != 'cancelled' || !changed().hasAny(['status'])))\n        || (role() == 'marketing' && request.resource.data.status == 'live' && oldListingStatus() in ['inProgress', 'progress', 'signed']\n            && !changed().hasAny(['prevStatus', 'signedAt', 'cancelledAt', 'cancelledBy', 'cancelledByUid', 'cancelReason']));\n    }\n\n    // ---- Paths and writes ----\n    function docPath(col, id)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/$(col)/$(id); }\n    function changed()           { return request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys(); }\n    function newKeysOnly(keys)   { return request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(keys); }\n    // Draft 0.57: a Director stamping states. Only `state` (a string) or `states` (a list) changes.\n    function stampOnly() {\n      return isDirector() && changed().hasOnly(['state', 'states'])\n        && request.resource.data.get('state', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('states', []) is list;\n    }\n    function createdNow(col, id) { return !exists(docPath(col, id)) && existsAfter(docPath(col, id)); }\n\n    // ---- Month-end: completion is per unit, statements/{unitId}_{month} ----\n    function statementPath(unitId, month) {\n      return /databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(unitId + '_' + month);\n    }\n    function unitCompleted(unitId, month) {\n      return (exists(statementPath(unitId, month))\n        && get(statementPath(unitId, month)).data.status == 'completed')\n        // Finance sent it to the Director: its numbers are frozen until approved, sent back or pulled back.\n        || (exists(approvalPath(unitId, month))\n        && get(approvalPath(unitId, month)).data.status == 'submitted');\n    }\n    function approvalPath(unitId, month) {\n      return /databases/$(database)/documents/approvals/$(unitId + '_' + month);\n    }\n    function unitMonthKeys() {\n      return ['propertyId', 'state', 'month', 'unitId', 'unitCode', 'engineVersion', 'inUnits', 'hasTerms', 'arrangement', 'arrangementType', 'fixedRentAmount',\n        'firstBookingId', 'row', 'noUnit', 'dash', 'statement', 'stale', 'dirtyRev', 'cleanRev', 'marks', 'computedAt', 'computedBy'];\n    }\n\n    // ---- Operations: inquiries, Create booking, direct bookings ----\n    function assignedToMe(inqId) { return get(docPath('offlineInquiries', inqId)).data.get('assignedToUid', null) == request.auth.uid; }\n    // True only inside the Create booking transaction: offline_{id} doesn't exist before and does after.\n    function bookingMadeNow(inqId) {\n      return !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId)) && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId));\n    }\n    // Operations write a tenant only through Create booking on an inquiry assigned to them, and only the tenant it points at.\n    function opsBooking(inqId, tenantId) {\n      return isOps() && inqId is string && assignedToMe(inqId) && bookingMadeNow(inqId)\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId)).data.tenantId == tenantId\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', inqId)).data.tenantId == tenantId;\n    }\n    // True only inside the transaction that creates this direct booking (offline_BK-0001) for this tenant.\n    function directBookingMadeNow(bookingId, tenantId) {\n      return bookingId is string && bookingId.matches('offline_BK-[0-9]+')\n        && !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId))\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.tenantId == tenantId\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n    }\n\n    // ---- Issues: the tag each role answers to ('Admin' has no sign-in role yet) ----\n    function myIssueTag() {\n      return { 'finance': 'Finance', 'it': 'IT', 'hr': 'HR', 'operations': 'Operations', 'procurement': 'Procurement', 'marketing': 'Marketing' }\n        .get(role(), exists(roleDoc(role())) ? get(roleDoc(role())).data.get('name', '-') : '-');   // a role made on the Roles page is tagged by its name\n    }\n    function canSeeIssue(d) { return anyStaff() && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in d.tags || d.raisedByUid == request.auth.uid); }\n\n    // ---- Complaints ----\n    function complaintAfter(id) { return getAfter(docPath('complaints', id)).data; }\n    function complaintNow(id)   { return get(docPath('complaints', id)).data; }\n    // Draft 0.38: a Director complaint is between the Directors and the HR person who sent it (fromId), not all of HR\n    // Draft 0.40: reads the complaint and the role once each (fewer get() calls; Firestore caps them per request)\n    function dirSide(id) {\n      let c = complaintNow(id);\n      let r = role();\n      return c.kind == 'director' && (r == 'director' || (r == 'hr' && c.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid));\n    }\n\n    // ================= Shared: private data, accounts, counters, logs =================\n\n    // Personal data lives only in {doc}/private/main. IT never reads it. Complaint text (HR/Directors), new owner\n    // listings' contact details (Director/Procurement) and COH marks (evaluator + HR/Director, Draft 0.32) have\n    // their own rules below.\n    match /{parent=**}/private/{docId} {\n      allow read, write: if finOrDir() && parent[0] != 'complaints' && parent[0] != 'newOwnerListings'\n        && parent[0] != 'cohEvaluations';\n      // Returning tenant search: collectionGroup('private') where kind == 'tenant'. kind is written only on\n      // tenants/{id}/private/main; Operations can't add it to an inquiry's private doc.\n      allow read: if (isOps() || finOrDir()) && resource.data.get('kind', '') == 'tenant';\n    }\n\n    match /users/{uid} {\n      // Page ticks, when saved, are a list.\n      function permsOk() { return !('perms' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.perms is list; }\n      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || staffAdmin() || isIT());\n      // Agreement renewals: everyone picks who is in charge of an agreement from the staff list.\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if permsOk() && (isDirector() || (isHR() && request.resource.data.role != 'director'));\n      // A Director cannot remove their own Director role or switch themselves off (no lock-out).\n      allow update: if isDirector() && permsOk() && (uid != request.auth.uid\n        || (request.resource.data.role == 'director' && request.resource.data.get('active', true) == true));\n      // HR: anyone except Directors and themselves, and never to Director.\n      allow update: if isHR() && permsOk() && uid != request.auth.uid\n        && resource.data.role != 'director' && request.resource.data.role != 'director';\n      // Sign-in stamps lastLoginAt on your own record (Team activity).\n      allow update: if signedIn() && request.auth.uid == uid && changed().hasOnly(['lastLoginAt']);\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Roles page (Director only). Everyone signed in reads, so the app can show names and usual pages after sign-in.\n    match /roles/{rid} {\n      allow read: if signedIn();\n      allow create, update: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.perms is list && rid != 'director';\n      allow delete: if isDirector() && rid != 'director';\n    }\n\n    match /config/{docId} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow write: if isDirector();\n    }\n\n    // Unit types added with \"+ Add type\" on Add unit: anyone who can add or edit units may add to the list.\n    match /config/unitTypes {\n      allow write: if (portfolioEditor() || portfolioAdder() || isMkt())\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['list']) && request.resource.data.list is list && request.resource.data.list.size() < 100;\n    }\n\n    // Numbered IDs (LD-, TEN-, IS-, BK-, CP-, DC-, NL-): taken one at a time inside a transaction.\n    match /counters/{name} {\n      allow read: if (name == 'offlineInquiries' && finOrDir())\n        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))\n        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff());\n      allow create: if request.resource.data.next == 2 && (\n           (name == 'offlineInquiries' && isDirector())\n        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))\n        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff()));\n      allow update: if request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1 && (\n           (name == 'offlineInquiries' && isDirector())\n        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))\n        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff()));\n      // Direct bookings.\n      allow read: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps());\n      allow create: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps()) && request.resource.data.next == 2;\n      allow update: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps()) && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;\n      // Complaints.\n      allow read: if name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff();\n      allow read: if name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir();\n      allow create: if ((name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff()) || (name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir()))\n        && request.resource.data.next == 2;\n      allow update: if ((name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff()) || (name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir()))\n        && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;\n      // Salary advances (Draft 0.42).\n      allow read: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff();\n      allow create: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff() && request.resource.data.next == 2;\n      allow update: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff() && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;\n      // New owner listings.\n      allow read: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor();\n      allow create: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor() && request.resource.data.next == 2;\n      allow update: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor() && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // What's New: every staff member reads the updates; only a Director posts, edits or deletes them.\n    match /updates/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update, delete: if isDirector();\n    }\n\n    // HR Announcements (Draft 0.37, 5 Nov 2026). Posted by HR and Directors to Everyone or chosen roles (role ids).\n    match /announcements/{id} {\n      function annPoster() { return isHR() || isDirector(); }\n      function annOk() {\n        return request.resource.data.title is string && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 150\n          && request.resource.data.message is string && request.resource.data.message.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.message.size() <= 5000\n          && request.resource.data.audience is list && request.resource.data.audience.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.audience.size() <= 40\n          && request.resource.data.get('pinned', false) is bool\n          && request.resource.data.get('files', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('files', []).size() <= 10;\n      }\n      allow read: if annPoster() || (anyStaff() && resource.data.audience.hasAny([role(), 'everyone']));\n      allow create: if annPoster() && annOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if annPoster() && annOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy\n        && request.resource.data.createdAt == resource.data.createdAt;\n      allow delete: if annPoster();\n\n      // Opened: once per person (no update), only for an announcement meant for them\n      match /views/{uid} {\n        function annForMe() {\n          return get(/databases/$(database)/documents/announcements/$(id)).data.audience.hasAny([role(), 'everyone']);\n        }\n        allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || isHR() || isDirector());\n        allow create: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid && annForMe()\n          && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['viewedAt', 'name', 'role'])\n          && request.resource.data.viewedAt == request.time;\n        allow delete: if isHR() || isDirector();\n      }\n    }\n    // Each person's own list of announcements they have opened (dashboard banner, Unread filter)\n    match /announcementReads/{uid} {\n      allow read: if signedIn() && request.auth.uid == uid;\n      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['ids']) && request.resource.data.ids is map;\n    }\n\n    // Every role writes its own audit entries; an anonymous complaint is logged with NO uid.\n    match /auditLog/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff() || isHR();\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == null && request.resource.data.userName == 'Anonymous'\n        && request.resource.data.role == null && request.resource.data.action == 'complaint.create';\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    match /accessLog/{id} {\n      allow read: if isDirector() || isIT();\n      allow create: if isIT() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Appearance: userPrefs/{uid} = { brand, mode, custom, updatedAt }. Each person reads and writes only their own.\n    match /userPrefs/{uid} {\n      allow read, create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Profile pictures: avatars/{uid} = { src, updatedAt }, a 128 px square data URL. Each person writes only their own.\n    match /avatars/{uid} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid\n        && newKeysOnly(['src', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.src is string && request.resource.data.src.size() <= 60000\n        && request.resource.data.src.matches('^data:image/(webp|jpeg|png);base64,.*')\n        && request.resource.data.updatedAt == request.time;\n      allow delete: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid;\n    }\n\n    // Brand logos: brandLogos/light and brandLogos/dark, a data URL each (<= 512 px). Director edits.\n    match /brandLogos/{key} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if isDirector() && key in ['light', 'dark']\n        && request.resource.data.src is string && request.resource.data.src.size() <= 280000\n        && request.resource.data.src.matches('^data:image/(png|webp);base64,.*');\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ================= Setup data (Portfolio) =================\n    // Finance/Directors write. Operations, Procurement and Marketing read the parents only (no terms, rates or\n    // owners' private data). Operations and Marketing may also create properties, units and owners (create only, never edit).\n    // Version documents are add-only: a change is a new document.\n\n    match /properties/{propertyId} {\n      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();\n      allow write: if portfolioEditor();\n      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['name', 'code', 'state', 'info', 'active', 'createdAt', 'createdBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.code is string\n        && (!('info' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['address', 'city', 'state', 'ezeeAccount', 'ezeeName']));\n      // The batch that adds a unit notes it on its property (summaryMarks); the only change Operations may make.\n      allow update: if portfolioAdder() && changed().hasOnly(['summaryMarks']);\n      // Marketing also edit the name and details (Khairul 27 Oct); never the short code or anything money.\n      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['name', 'info', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'summaryMarks'])\n        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['address', 'city', 'state', 'ezeeAccount', 'ezeeName']);\n      match /rateVersions/{v} {\n        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();\n        allow create: if portfolioEditor() && request.resource.data.reason is string;\n        // Operations: only the default OTA rates, only in the batch that creates the property.\n        allow create: if portfolioAdder() && v == '2000-01_default' && createdNow('properties', propertyId)\n          && request.resource.data.effectiveFrom == '2000-01' && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n          && newKeysOnly(['effectiveFrom', 'ota', 'earlyCheckInToOwner', 'tourismTaxPerNight', 'reason', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'createdAt']);\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // One set of fees and rates for every property (Draft 0.60). Add-only versions, like rateVersions above.\n    match /sharedRates/{v} {\n      allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();\n      allow create: if portfolioEditor() && request.resource.data.reason is string;\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    match /units/{unitId} {\n      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();\n      allow create, update: if portfolioEditor();\n      allow delete: if isDirector();   // safe delete: the page only offers it for units with no history\n      // Operations: no terms (arrangement, fixed rent, fees).\n      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'state', 'unitCode', 'ezeeRoomMatch', 'aliases', 'ownerId', 'info', 'active',\n          'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && exists(docPath('properties', request.resource.data.propertyId))\n        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['type', 'bedrooms', 'bathrooms', 'sizeSqft', 'carParks', 'tnb', 'water', 'wifi', 'sewerage', 'jmb']);\n      // Marketing edit unit details and eZee names; not the owner link, status or terms.\n      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['aliases', 'info', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['type', 'bedrooms', 'bathrooms', 'sizeSqft', 'carParks', 'tnb', 'water', 'wifi', 'sewerage', 'jmb']);\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      match /terms/{v} {\n        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();\n        allow create: if portfolioEditor() && request.resource.data.reason is string;\n        allow update: if false;\n        allow delete: if isDirector();   // only when a unit is safe-deleted\n      }\n      match /ownership/{id} {\n        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();\n        allow write: if portfolioEditor();\n      }\n    }\n\n    // The owner parent holds bankLast4 (not shown to portfolio viewers); Operations create it with none.\n    match /owners/{ownerId} {\n      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();\n      allow create, update: if portfolioEditor();\n      allow delete: if isDirector();   // safe delete: the page only offers it for owners with no units\n      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['code', 'active', 'bankLast4', 'states', 'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.get('bankLast4', null) == null\n        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);\n      // Draft 0.57: an owner's `states` (the states of their units) is worked out again after Operations or Marketing save a unit\n      allow update: if (portfolioAdder() || isMkt()) && changed().hasOnly(['states']) && request.resource.data.states is list\n        && request.resource.data.states.size() <= 16;\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      // Operations write name and contact details once, in the batch that creates the owner, and never read them back.\n      match /private/{docId} {\n        // Portfolio Edit: names, contact and bank details.\n        allow read, write: if portfolioEditor() && docId == 'main';\n        allow create: if portfolioAdder() && docId == 'main' && createdNow('owners', ownerId)\n          && newKeysOnly(['fullName', 'ic', 'email', 'phone', 'dob', 'whatsapp', 'wechat', 'address', 'coOwners', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])\n          && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid;\n        // Marketing read and edit names and contact details (Khairul 27 Oct). Bank fields share this document: the\n        // page hides them and Marketing can't change them.\n        allow read: if isMkt() && docId == 'main';\n        // Draft 0.58: Operations read it too, for owner names (the page shows only the name)\n        allow read: if portfolioAdder() && docId == 'main';\n        allow update: if isMkt() && docId == 'main' && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid\n          && changed().hasOnly(['fullName', 'ic', 'email', 'phone', 'dob', 'whatsapp', 'wechat', 'address', 'coOwners', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);\n      }\n    }\n\n    match /agreements/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();\n      allow write: if portfolioEditor();\n    }\n\n    // ================= Finance: bookings and month-end =================\n\n    // eZee uploads. Operations read the latest for \"Last eZee upload\" on their dashboard.\n    match /importBatches/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff() || isOps() || opsRole();\n      allow create: if finOrDir();\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Locked months are protected by the app posting changes as adjustments (CSV-13); Edit on a completed month goes\n    // through a Director Override revision.\n    // ===== Role dashboards (dash): Operations read today's check-ins/outs (parent docs only, no write).\n    match /bookings/{reservationNo} {\n      allow read: if staff() || isOps() || opsRole();\n      allow create, update: if finOrDir();\n      // Draft 0.24 (Khairul): only a booking already removed by hand on Month-end (cancelled + removedByHand), by Finance/Director\n      allow delete: if finOrDir() && resource.data.status == 'cancelled' && resource.data.get('removedByHand', null) != null;\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n    }\n\n    // Each unit's payout per month: completed statements, and Finance's past statements uploaded as reference.\n    match /payoutHistory/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create, update: if finOrDir();\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if isDirector();\n    }\n\n    // months/{propertyId}_{month}: open -> partial -> completed as units are completed, plus a `summary` field.\n    match /months/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];\n      // Once completed, only a Director may change the status (Override / unit reopen).\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && (resource.data.status != 'completed' || isDirector())\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];\n      // Summary-only writes, on any month.\n      allow create: if finOrDir()\n        && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'state', 'month', 'summary'])\n        && id == request.resource.data.propertyId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;\n      // Pool Sharing check (Draft 0.46): \"Confirmed 0 bookings\" per unit, with who and when (poolZero only).\n      allow create: if finOrDir() && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'state', 'month', 'poolZero'])\n        && id == request.resource.data.propertyId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && changed().hasOnly(['poolZero', 'state']);\n      allow update: if finOrDir()\n        && changed().hasOnly(['propertyId', 'state', 'month', 'summary'])\n        && request.resource.data.propertyId == resource.data.get('propertyId', request.resource.data.propertyId)\n        && request.resource.data.month == resource.data.get('month', request.resource.data.month);\n      // Approve & complete on a summary-only month document (no status yet means open).\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && resource.data.get('status', 'open') != 'completed'\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ===== Month summaries (scale): unitMonths/{unitId}_{month}, worked out once by lib/summaries.js. Never deleted.\n    match /unitMonths/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create, update: if finOrDir()\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(unitMonthKeys())\n        && request.resource.data.propertyId is string && request.resource.data.month is string && request.resource.data.unitId is string\n        && id == request.resource.data.unitId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    match /expenses/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create: if finOrDir()\n        && !unitCompleted(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month);\n      // Automatic Brought Forward lines are only rewritten by Approve & complete / Reopen (auto stays true).\n      allow update: if finOrDir()\n        && (resource.data.auto != true || request.resource.data.auto == true)\n        && !unitCompleted(resource.data.unitId, resource.data.month)\n        && !unitCompleted(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month)\n        && request.resource.data.month == resource.data.month;\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;   // \"Remove\" sets deleted = true\n    }\n\n    match /statements/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      // Approve & complete, one unit at a time. Only a Director completes (Finance sends to the Director: approvals below).\n      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.revision == 1 && request.resource.data.status == 'completed';\n      // Director reopens one unit: same revision, status 'reopened', and the revision is saved first.\n      allow update: if isDirector()\n        && resource.data.status == 'completed' && request.resource.data.status == 'reopened'\n        && resource.data.get('paymentStatus', '') != 'paid'\n        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision\n        && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(id)/revisions/$(string(resource.data.revision)));\n      // Director Override (completing a reopened unit again): revision goes up by one, the old one saved first.\n      allow update: if isDirector()\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'completed'\n        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision + 1\n        && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(id)/revisions/$(string(resource.data.revision)));\n      // Owner payment (Draft 0.18, Invoices & Receipts): Finance or a Director marks a completed statement Paid (pay slip in Drive);\n      // only a Director sets it back to pending (Undo payment). Nothing else on the statement changes.\n      allow update: if (isDirector() || isFinance())\n        && resource.data.status == 'completed' && request.resource.data.status == 'completed'\n        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision\n        && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['paymentStatus', 'paidDate', 'paidAmount', 'paidRef', 'paidBy', 'paidByName', 'paidAt', 'payUndoReason', 'payUndoBy', 'payUndoByName', 'payUndoAt'])\n        && (request.resource.data.paymentStatus == 'paid' || (isDirector() && request.resource.data.paymentStatus == 'pending'));\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n      match /revisions/{rev} {\n        allow read: if staff();\n        allow create: if isDirector();\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Finance sends a unit's statement to the Director (Statement Approvals page). id = unitId_month, same as statements.\n    // submitted -> approved (Director completes it, same batch as the statement) or returned (Director, reason) or\n    // withdrawn (Finance pulls it back, reason). Returned / withdrawn can be sent again. After a Director reopen, an approved\n    // one can be sent again too.\n    match /approvals/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && id == request.resource.data.unitId + '_' + request.resource.data.month\n        && request.resource.data.submittedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && (!exists(statementPath(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month))\n          || get(statementPath(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month)).data.status == 'reopened');\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted' && request.resource.data.submittedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && (resource.data.status in ['returned', 'withdrawn']\n          || (resource.data.status == 'approved' && get(statementPath(resource.data.unitId, resource.data.month)).data.status == 'reopened'));\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && resource.data.status == 'submitted' && request.resource.data.status == 'withdrawn'\n        && request.resource.data.withdrawReason is string && request.resource.data.withdrawReason.size() > 0;\n      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && (request.resource.data.status == 'approved'\n          || (request.resource.data.status == 'returned' && request.resource.data.returnReason is string && request.resource.data.returnReason.size() > 0));\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    match /exports/{id} {\n      allow read: if staff();\n      allow create: if finOrDir() || can('reports.edit');\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ================= Operations: inquiries, tenants, offline bookings, Issues =================\n\n    // Directors log inquiries; Finance and Directors read all; IT reads the parent only (no contact details);\n    // Operations read and update only the ones assigned to them.\n    match /offlineInquiries/{id} {\n      allow read: if finOrDir() || isIT() || (isOps() && resource.data.assignedToUid == request.auth.uid);\n      allow create: if isDirector()\n        && request.resource.data.loggedByUid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested']\n        && request.resource.data.get('bookingId', null) == null;\n      // Directors: anything, including (re)assigning.\n      allow update: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked'];\n      // Finance: status, notes, booking; not the assignee.\n      allow update: if isFinance()\n        && !changed().hasAny(['assignedToUid', 'assignedToName', 'loggedByUid', 'loggedByName', 'createdAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked'];\n      // The assignee: status, history and (only in Create booking) the tenant and booking links.\n      allow update: if isOps() && resource.data.assignedToUid == request.auth.uid\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'history', 'updatedAt', 'tenantId', 'bookingId'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked']\n        && (bookingMadeNow(id)\n            || (!changed().hasAny(['tenantId', 'bookingId']) && (request.resource.data.status != 'booked' || resource.data.status == 'booked')));\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n      // Contact details: Finance/Directors through the catch-all; the assignee here.\n      match /private/{docId} {\n        allow read: if isOps() && assignedToMe(id);\n        allow create, update: if isOps() && assignedToMe(id)\n          && newKeysOnly(['contactName', 'phone', 'phoneKey', 'email']);\n        allow delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Written by Finance/Directors, and by Operations only inside Create booking (opsBooking, lastInquiryId)\n    // or a direct booking (directBookingMadeNow, lastBookingId).\n    match /tenants/{tenantId} {\n      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps();\n      allow create, update: if finOrDir();\n      allow create, update: if opsBooking(request.resource.data.get('lastInquiryId', null), tenantId)\n        && (resource == null || changed().hasOnly(['status', 'states', 'lastInquiryId', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']));\n      allow create, update: if isOps() && directBookingMadeNow(request.resource.data.get('lastBookingId', null), tenantId)\n        && (resource == null || changed().hasOnly(['status', 'states', 'lastBookingId', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']));\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n      match /private/{docId} {\n        allow read: if isOps();\n        allow create, update: if opsBooking(getAfter(docPath('tenants', tenantId)).data.get('lastInquiryId', null), tenantId);\n        allow create, update: if isOps()\n          && directBookingMadeNow(getAfter(docPath('tenants', tenantId)).data.get('lastBookingId', null), tenantId);\n        allow delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Offline payments (Finance > Offline Payments): submitted and checked by Finance/Director.\n    // View and Edit are separate ticks: Offline Payments View reads; Offline Payments Edit creates and changes.\n    match /offlinePayments/{id} {\n      allow read: if can('offlinePayments.view') || can('offlinePayments.edit');\n      allow create: if can('offlinePayments.edit') && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status in ['Pending', 'Checked', 'Unknown'];\n      allow update: if can('offlinePayments.edit');\n      // The Booking Form saves the booking's payment here (Pending), in the same write as the booking itself.\n      allow create: if (isOps() || finOrDir()) && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status == 'Pending'\n        && request.resource.data.bookingId is string && !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', request.resource.data.bookingId))\n        && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', request.resource.data.bookingId));\n      // Operations fill in a payment that has no receipt (status Unknown): saving it makes it Edited, and Finance is told.\n      allow update: if role() == 'operations' && can('offlinePayments.view') && resource.data.status == 'Unknown' && request.resource.data.status == 'Edited'\n        && !changed().hasAny(['createdBy', 'createdAt', 'submittedByName', 'verifiedByName', 'verifiedDate', 'remarks']);\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n    // Utility bills logged against an offline booking (Operations > Booking Forms > Utility Lodgment Form); one per booking.\n    match /utilityBills/{bookingId} {\n      // Booking Forms View is the only tick that page has, so it gives the form (read, save and update a bill).\n      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view');\n      allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view')) && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && exists(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId));\n      allow update: if finOrDir() || can('bookingForms.view');\n      // Draft 0.36: removed with its booking, only while the booking is cancelled.\n      allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && get(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n    }\n\n    // Not the bookings collection: Finance's month-end reads bookings, and these are paid from eZee.\n    // offline_{inquiryId} from Create booking, or offline_BK-0001 for a direct booking (no inquiry).\n    match /offlineBookings/{bookingId} {\n      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps() || portfolioViewer();\n      allow create: if finOrDir() && bookingId == 'offline_' + request.resource.data.inquiryId;\n      allow update: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.inquiryId == resource.data.inquiryId;\n      // Operations: Create booking on their own inquiry (the inquiry must point back and be booked in the same write).\n      allow create: if isOps() && bookingId == 'offline_' + request.resource.data.inquiryId\n        && assignedToMe(request.resource.data.inquiryId)\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', request.resource.data.inquiryId)).data.bookingId == bookingId\n        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', request.resource.data.inquiryId)).data.status == 'booked';\n      // ...and adding the eZee reservation no. later.\n      allow update: if isOps() && assignedToMe(resource.data.inquiryId)\n        && changed().hasOnly(['ezeeReservationNo', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);\n      // Operations edit any booking's details (Portfolio > Bookings > open a booking); who, source and the inquiry link stay as they were.\n      allow update: if isOps() && !changed().hasAny(['createdBy', 'createdAt', 'source', 'inquiryId', 'bookingNo', 'tenantId', 'propertyId', 'unitId']);\n      // Direct booking (Portfolio > Bookings > + New booking).\n      allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && bookingId.matches('offline_BK-[0-9]+')\n        && request.resource.data.source == 'direct' && request.resource.data.inquiryId == null\n        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.tenantId is string\n        && getAfter(docPath('tenants', request.resource.data.tenantId)) != null;\n      // Willow Booking Details bulk upload (Portfolio > Bulk Upload): Finance or a Director, offline_{booking no.} such as offline_DM-014.\n      allow create: if finOrDir() && bookingId.matches('offline_[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9]+') && request.resource.data.source == 'import'\n        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      // Draft 0.36: delete for good, only a cancelled booking (the page also checks no payment is recorded).\n      allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && resource.data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      // Door passcodes for the booking (Booking Form).\n      match /private/{doc} {\n        allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps();\n        allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId));\n        allow update: if finOrDir() || isOps();\n        allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && get(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Issues: seen by the tagged roles, the person who raised it and Directors. Every role raises tickets.\n    // Completed tickets are locked.\n    match /issues/{id} {\n      allow read: if canSeeIssue(resource.data);\n      allow create: if anyStaff()\n        && request.resource.data.raisedByUid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'open'\n        && request.resource.data.tags is list && request.resource.data.tags.size() > 0;\n      // A comment (anyone who can see it): counters, last poster and the ticket's audit trail.\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && canSeeIssue(resource.data) && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']\n        && changed().hasOnly(['replyCount', 'linkCount', 'lastBy', 'audit', 'updatedAt']);\n      // In progress, tags and Mark completed: Directors and the tagged roles.\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']\n        && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in resource.data.tags)\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'tags', 'type', 'doneAt', 'doneBy', 'doneByUid', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])\n        && (!('type' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.type in ['customer', 'inhouse'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress', 'done']\n        && request.resource.data.tags is list && request.resource.data.tags.size() > 0;\n      // Draft 0.47: title, description, property and the task system column (tmsStatus), from the Issues page or the task system (TMS),\n      // with or without a status change: Directors and the tagged roles, while the ticket is Open or In progress.\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']\n        && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in resource.data.tags)\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'doneAt', 'doneBy', 'doneByUid', 'title', 'body', 'property', 'propertyId', 'state', 'tmsStatus', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress', 'done']\n        && (request.resource.data.status != 'done' || request.resource.data.get('doneByUid', '') == request.auth.uid)\n        && request.resource.data.get('title', '') is string\n        && request.resource.data.get('title', '').size() > 0 && request.resource.data.get('title', '').size() <= 200\n        && request.resource.data.get('body', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('body', '').size() <= 5000\n        && request.resource.data.get('property', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('property', '').size() <= 80\n        && (!('tmsStatus' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.tmsStatus is map);\n      // Delete ticket: Directors only, any status. Marked deleted with a reason, never removed; nothing changes it after.\n      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.status != 'deleted'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'deletedAt', 'deletedBy', 'deletedByUid', 'deleteReason', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'deleted'\n        && request.resource.data.deleteReason is string && request.resource.data.deleteReason.size() > 0;\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n      match /replies/{replyId} {\n        allow read: if canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data);\n        allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid\n          && canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data)\n          && get(docPath('issues', id)).data.status in ['open', 'progress'];\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Draft 0.20: quote and invoice for a ticket. Anyone who can see the ticket reads the quote and adds or edits it while\n    // it is Quoted or Rejected (it goes back to Quoted). Director and people with the Expenses Edit tick (Finance) approve,\n    // reject, add the invoice (which also writes an expense line, expenses rules above) and mark it paid.\n    // Always charged to the unit's owner. Nothing changes once the vendor is Paid.\n    match /issueQuotes/{id} {\n      function priceAccess() { return isDirector() || can('expenses.edit'); }\n      function ticketOk() {\n        return exists(docPath('issues', id)) && get(docPath('issues', id)).data.status != 'deleted'\n          && canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data);\n      }\n      function quoteKeys() {\n        return ['issueId', 'propertyId', 'state', 'unitId', 'unitCode', 'chargeTo', 'vendor', 'items', 'total', 'notes', 'status', 'rejectReason',\n          'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'history', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'];\n      }\n      function quoteOk() {\n        return request.resource.data.issueId == id && request.resource.data.chargeTo == 'owner'\n          && request.resource.data.items is list && request.resource.data.items.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.items.size() <= 20;\n      }\n      allow read: if anyStaff() && ticketOk();\n      // Any staff member: add a quote, or edit one that is Quoted or Rejected. It is saved as Quoted.\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'quoted' && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(quoteKeys());\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()\n        && resource.data.status in ['quoted', 'rejected'] && request.resource.data.status == 'quoted'\n        && changed().hasOnly(quoteKeys());\n      // Director and Finance: every step.\n      allow create, update: if priceAccess() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['quoted', 'approved', 'invoiced', 'paid', 'rejected']\n        && (resource == null || resource.data.status != 'paid');\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Draft 0.24 (Khairul): push notifications. One document per device (the id is the Firebase Cloud Messaging token), holding\n    // the uid of the person signed in there. A browser that someone else signs into is taken over by them (same device).\n    // Only that person reads or removes it; api/push.js reads them with the service account to send pushes.\n    match /pushTokens/{token} {\n      allow read, delete: if anyStaff() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['uid', 'role', 'device', 'updatedAt']);\n    }\n\n    // Notifications: one document per recipient target. recipientUid = one person; recipientRole = everyone in\n    // that role (read state is per person in readBy). Both keys are always written, the unused one as null.\n    // Anyone signed in with a role may send one, but only as themselves and only with an in-app link.\n    // ONE exception (Draft 0.10): an anonymous complaint alert has no sender (createdByUid null, createdByName ''),\n    // and may only go to HR with type 'complaint', so the sender of an anonymous complaint cannot be traced from it.\n    // Stronger protection against spoofing needs a Cloud Function that sends them.\n    match /notifications/{id} {\n      function onlyMine(before, after) {\n        return after is list\n          && after.toSet().difference(before.toSet()).hasOnly([request.auth.uid])\n          && before.toSet().difference(after.toSet()).hasOnly([request.auth.uid]);\n      }\n      allow read: if anyStaff() && (resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid || resource.data.recipientRole == role());\n      allow create: if anyStaff()\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['recipientUid', 'recipientRole', 'title', 'message', 'type', 'link', 'refId',\n          'readBy', 'starredBy', 'createdByUid', 'createdByName', 'createdAt'])\n        && (\n          request.resource.data.createdByUid == request.auth.uid\n          // Anonymous complaint alert: no sender recorded, HR only, complaint type only\n          || (request.resource.data.createdByUid == null\n              && request.resource.data.createdByName == ''\n              && request.resource.data.recipientRole == 'hr'\n              && request.resource.data.type == 'complaint')\n        )\n        && request.resource.data.readBy == []\n        && request.resource.data.get('starredBy', []) == []\n        && request.resource.data.title is string && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 200\n        && request.resource.data.message is string && request.resource.data.message.size() <= 600\n        && request.resource.data.link is string && request.resource.data.link.matches('/.*')\n        && ((request.resource.data.recipientUid is string && request.resource.data.recipientRole == null)\n          || (request.resource.data.recipientUid == null\n            && (request.resource.data.recipientRole in ['director', 'finance', 'it', 'hr', 'operations', 'procurement', 'marketing']\n              // Draft 0.21: a role made on the Roles page (e.g. Maintenance)\n              || (request.resource.data.recipientRole is string && exists(roleDoc(request.resource.data.recipientRole))))));\n      // Read, unread, star and hide (Draft 0.22): the recipient adds or removes only their own uid in readBy / starredBy / hiddenBy.\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && (resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid || resource.data.recipientRole == role())\n        && changed().hasOnly(['readBy', 'starredBy', 'hiddenBy'])\n        && onlyMine(resource.data.readBy, request.resource.data.readBy)\n        && onlyMine(resource.data.get('starredBy', []), request.resource.data.get('starredBy', []))\n        && onlyMine(resource.data.get('hiddenBy', []), request.resource.data.get('hiddenBy', []));\n      // Draft 0.22: a notification sent to one person may be deleted by that person (Clear on the Notifications page).\n      // Team notifications are never deleted (others still need them): they are hidden per person above.\n      allow delete: if anyStaff() && resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid;\n    }\n\n    // ================= HR: SOPs, Playbook, onboarding, complaints =================\n\n    // sops/{key}. Everyone reads; HR and Directors edit and soft-delete (deleted: true). Never removed.\n    match /sops/{sopKey} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      // Any SOP key: lower case, digits and dashes, 2 to 40 long (the first four keep their keys).\n      allow create, update: if can('sops.edit') && sopKey.matches('^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,39}$')\n        && request.resource.data.updatedByUid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.steps is list && request.resource.data.steps.size() > 0\n        && (!('title' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.title is string\n          && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 80))\n        && (!('sub' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.sub is string && request.resource.data.sub.size() <= 200))\n        && (!('icon' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.icon is string && request.resource.data.icon.size() <= 30))\n        // Deleting is a soft delete with a reason.\n        && (!('deleted' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.deleted == true\n          && request.resource.data.deleteReason is string && request.resource.data.deleteReason.size() > 0));\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // playbook/businessModel and playbook/onboarding. Everyone reads; HR and Directors edit.\n    match /playbook/{pageId} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if can('playbook.edit') && pageId in ['businessModel', 'onboarding']\n        && request.resource.data.updatedByUid == request.auth.uid;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Onboarding ticks: each person writes their own; HR and Directors read everyone's.\n    match /onboardingProgress/{uid} {\n      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || hrOrDir());\n      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid\n        && newKeysOnly(['ticks', 'updatedAt']) && request.resource.data.ticks is map;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // complaints/{id}, kind 'staff' (any staff -> HR) or 'director' (HR -> Directors). The parent holds only ref, kind,\n    // date, createdAt and status/read (plus fromId on a named staff complaint); the text is in private/main.\n    // An anonymous staff complaint has no fromId or fromName anywhere.\n    match /complaints/{id} {\n      // HR reads everything. Directors read only Director complaints (never staff complaints).\n      allow read: if (isHR() && (resource.data.kind == 'staff' || resource.data.fromId == request.auth.uid)) || (isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director');\n      // The sender of a named complaint follows it under My complaints.\n      allow read: if signedIn() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;\n      // An anonymous sender's browser keeps the (random) id and reads only the status.\n      allow get: if anyStaff() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.anonymous == true;\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.kind == 'staff' && request.resource.data.status == 'new'\n        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'kind', 'date', 'createdAt', 'status', 'anonymous', 'fromId'])\n        && ((request.resource.data.anonymous == false && request.resource.data.fromId == request.auth.uid)\n          || (request.resource.data.anonymous == true && !('fromId' in request.resource.data)));\n      // Director complaints: HR sends (Directors too, so the form can be tried out).\n      allow create: if hrOrDir() && request.resource.data.kind == 'director' && request.resource.data.read == false\n        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'kind', 'date', 'createdAt', 'read', 'fromId']) && request.resource.data.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;\n      // Draft 0.25: HR opening a New staff complaint marks it Read by HR; the only change ever made to a staff complaint.\n      allow update: if isHR() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.status == 'new'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'readAt', 'readBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'read' && request.resource.data.readBy == request.auth.uid;\n      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): HR moves a staff complaint to Read by HR, In review or Closed (Reopen = back to In review).\n      allow update: if isHR() && resource.data.kind == 'staff'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'statusAt', 'statusBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['read', 'review', 'closed'] && request.resource.data.statusBy == request.auth.uid;\n      // Only a Director opening a Director complaint marks it read.\n      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['read', 'readAt', 'readBy', 'status'])\n        && request.resource.data.read == true && request.resource.data.readBy == request.auth.uid\n        && (!changed().hasAny(['status']) || request.resource.data.status == 'read');\n      // Draft 0.30: the Directors move a Director complaint to Read by the Directors, In review or Closed (Reopen = In review).\n      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'statusAt', 'statusBy'])\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['read', 'review', 'closed'] && request.resource.data.statusBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow delete: if false;\n      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): the conversation with the sender. HR reads all; the named sender reads theirs; an anonymous\n      // sender's browser reads by the (random) id, like the status. HR writes any time (a closing note goes with the Close);\n      // the NAMED sender writes back while it isn't Closed. Text up to 2000 characters (or photos only), never changed.\n      match /thread/{tid} {\n        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff')\n          || (signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid)\n          || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true);\n        allow create: if complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff'\n          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'by', 'byName', 'byUid', 'closing', 'imageIds', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000\n          && (request.resource.data.text.size() > 0\n            || (request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() > 0))\n          && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() <= 5\n          && ((request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid\n              && ((isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr')\n                || (request.resource.data.by == 'sender' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid\n                    && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed' && !('closing' in request.resource.data))))\n            // Draft 0.49: the anonymous sender (no uid or name saved)\n            || (anyStaff() && request.resource.data.by == 'sender' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true\n                && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed' && !('byUid' in request.resource.data) && !('byName' in request.resource.data)\n                && !('closing' in request.resource.data)));\n        // Draft 0.29: a Director complaint's conversation is between HR and the Directors\n        allow read: if dirSide(id);\n        // Draft 0.30: a closing note (closing) comes only from the Directors; HR can't write once it is Closed.\n        allow create: if dirSide(id)\n          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'by', 'byName', 'byUid', 'imageIds', 'closing', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000\n          && (request.resource.data.text.size() > 0\n            || (request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() > 0))\n          && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() <= 5\n          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid\n          && ((isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr' && complaintNow(id).get('status', '') != 'closed' && !('closing' in request.resource.data))\n            || (isDirector() && request.resource.data.by == 'director'));\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): photos. Read by the same people as the conversation. Added with the complaint by its sender\n      // (an anonymous complaint: no uid, and only in the first 15 minutes after it was sent), or with a reply by HR or the\n      // named sender (not once Closed). Each record is one image, at most ~700 KB of text.\n      match /images/{img} {\n        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff')\n          || (signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid)\n          || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true);\n        allow create: if complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff'\n          && newKeysOnly(['data', 'w', 'h', 'size', 'scope', 'threadId', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.data is string && request.resource.data.data.size() <= 700000\n          && ((request.resource.data.scope == 'complaint' && !('threadId' in request.resource.data)\n                && ((complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid)\n                  || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true && !('byUid' in request.resource.data)\n                      && request.time < complaintNow(id).createdAt + duration.value(15, 'm'))))\n            || (request.resource.data.scope == 'thread' && request.resource.data.threadId is string\n                && ((request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid\n                    && (isHR() || (complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed')))\n                  || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed'\n                    && !('byUid' in request.resource.data)))));\n        // Draft 0.29: Director complaints: HR and Directors read and add photos (with the complaint or a reply)\n        allow read: if dirSide(id);\n        allow create: if dirSide(id)\n          && newKeysOnly(['data', 'w', 'h', 'size', 'scope', 'threadId', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.data is string && request.resource.data.data.size() <= 700000\n          && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid\n          && (request.resource.data.scope == 'complaint' || (request.resource.data.scope == 'thread' && request.resource.data.threadId is string));\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      // Draft 0.48 (Khairul): documents on a staff complaint. The file is in HR's Google Drive; this is its name and id.\n      match /docs/{did} {\n        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff')\n          || (signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid)\n          || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true);\n        allow create: if complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff'\n          && newKeysOnly(['name', 'fileId', 'mimeType', 'by', 'byUid', 'threadId', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.name.size() <= 200\n          && request.resource.data.fileId is string && request.resource.data.fileId.matches('^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,64}$')\n          && ((isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr' && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid)\n            || (request.resource.data.by == 'sender' && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid\n                && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed')\n            // Draft 0.49: an anonymous sender any time while it isn't Closed (was the first 15 minutes only)\n            || (request.resource.data.by == 'anon' && anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true\n                && !('byUid' in request.resource.data) && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed'));\n        // Draft 0.49: Director complaints (HR's Drive). The Directors any time; the HR sender while it isn't Closed.\n        allow read: if dirSide(id);\n        allow create: if dirSide(id)\n          && newKeysOnly(['name', 'fileId', 'mimeType', 'by', 'byUid', 'threadId', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.name.size() <= 200\n          && request.resource.data.fileId is string && request.resource.data.fileId.matches('^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,64}$')\n          && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid\n          && ((isDirector() && request.resource.data.by == 'director')\n            || (isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr' && complaintNow(id).get('status', '') != 'closed'));\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): HR's own notes on a staff complaint; nobody else reads them.\n      // Draft 0.30: the Directors' own notes on a Director complaint; HR never reads those.\n      match /notes/{nid} {\n        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff') || (isDirector() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'director');\n        allow create: if ((isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff') || (isDirector() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'director'))\n          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'byName', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000\n          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid;\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      match /private/{docId} {\n        allow read: if isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff';\n        allow read: if dirSide(id);\n        // Draft 0.40 backup check: the HR sender reads their own private part by its own fromUid (no get() on the parent)\n        allow read: if isHR() && resource.data.get('fromUid', null) == request.auth.uid;\n        allow read: if signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;\n        // Written once, in the same transaction as the parent. Anonymous: no fromName.\n        allow create: if docId == 'main' && anyStaff()\n          && newKeysOnly(['subject', 'details', 'files', 'fromName', 'fromUid'])\n          && (!('fromUid' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.fromUid == request.auth.uid)\n          && ((complaintAfter(id).kind == 'staff'\n                && (complaintAfter(id).anonymous == true ? !('fromName' in request.resource.data) && !('fromUid' in request.resource.data) : complaintAfter(id).fromId == request.auth.uid))\n            || (complaintAfter(id).kind == 'director' && hrOrDir()));\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // ================= Procurement: New Owner Listings =================\n\n    // newOwnerListings/{NL-0001}: one new unit from service agreement to Live. New Owner Listings Edit creates and edits;\n    // anyone with the page ticked reads. Owner phone and email in private/main (editors; Operations with View read them).\n    match /newOwnerListings/{id} {\n      allow read: if listingViewer() || listingEditor();\n      allow create: if listingEditor() && id.matches('NL-[0-9]{4,}')\n        && request.resource.data.createdByUid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['inProgress', 'progress'];\n      allow update: if listingEditor()\n        && !changed().hasAny(['createdByUid', 'createdByName', 'createdAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.get('status', 'inProgress') in listingStatuses()\n        && listingStatusOk();\n      // Draft 0.57: Stamp states (a Director copies the property's state onto the record; nothing else changes)\n      allow update: if stampOnly();\n      allow delete: if false;\n      match /private/{docId} {\n        allow read: if listingMover() && listingViewer() && docId == 'main';\n        allow write: if listingMover() && listingEditor() && docId == 'main';\n      }\n    }\n\n    // ================= Performance management (Stage 1+2 security/revision fixes, 3 Nov 2026) =================\n    // performance.edit is not yet in presetFor()/PRESETS — until it's added, only the Director can write.\n    // Everyone reads quarter config (deadlines, status) so excluded employees can be told why they see nothing further.\n    function perfEdit() { return isDirector() || can('performance.edit'); }\n    // By business rule, Director/HR (performance.edit) may edit or delete a quarter's configuration at any\n    // lifecycle status, including finalized/archived — not restricted to draft. This is a deliberate choice,\n    // not an oversight: editing a quarter that's already in progress can change what a later recalculation\n    // produces, and deleting one does not cascade-delete its participants/evaluations/results (they stay\n    // queryable by quarterId even without a parent quarter doc). setStatus() still only touches status+stamp.\n    match /performanceQuarters/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if perfEdit();\n      allow delete: if perfEdit();\n    }\n\n    // Participation rosters are readable by every staff member, not just the participant themselves: COH\n    // evaluation requires every employee to see who else is eligible this quarter in order to rate them.\n    match /performanceParticipants/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit');\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // COH questions: everyone reads (so they know what they're being rated on); only performance.edit changes them.\n    // Confirmed business rule: COH questions are Director/HR only — not the generic performance.edit tick that\n    // gates other Performance admin actions, since question wording is a Code of Conduct/HR policy matter.\n    match /cohQuestions/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if hrOrDir();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // COH evaluations: evaluator identity is always visible to the evaluatee and to HR/Director (confirmed\n    // requirement, not an anonymous system). The id itself (quarterId_evaluatorUid_evaluateeUid) stops one\n    // evaluator from rating the same colleague twice under two different documents.\n    // The SCORE is not on this document (see private/scores below) — by business rule, the person being rated\n    // never sees the mark a specific evaluator gave them, only that the evaluation happened and who gave it.\n    match /cohEvaluations/{id} {\n      function evalDoc() { return /databases/$(database)/documents/cohEvaluations/$(id); }\n\n      // Director and HR always see every evaluation (Team overview monitoring), regardless of whether they\n      // hold the generic performance.edit tick — same confirmed business rule as cohQuestions above.\n      // (resource == null && anyStaff()): getEvaluation() probes this exact id to check \"have I already rated\n      // this colleague\" before the doc exists — without this clause that probe gets permission-denied instead\n      // of a normal exists:false, breaking \"Evaluate\" the first time anyone opens a colleague.\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || isHR() || can('performance.edit')\n        || resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid || resource.data.evaluateeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.evaluateeId != request.auth.uid\n        && id == request.resource.data.quarterId + '_' + request.resource.data.evaluatorId + '_' + request.resource.data.evaluateeId\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && !('ratings' in request.resource.data) && !('averageRating' in request.resource.data);\n      // Resubmit: same pair, saved back as 'submitted'. Draft 0.34: also allowed from 'approved', so an evaluator can\n      // answer questions added after they submitted; it then goes back to 'submitted' for HR/Director to review again.\n      // The marks themselves are protected in private/scores below (earlier answers can't be dropped once approved).\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid && resource.data.status in ['submitted', 'approved']\n        && request.resource.data.evaluatorId == resource.data.evaluatorId && request.resource.data.evaluateeId == resource.data.evaluateeId\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && !('ratings' in request.resource.data) && !('averageRating' in request.resource.data);\n      // HR/Director approve: only the review fields change.\n      allow update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit'))\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'reviewedBy', 'reviewedAt']) && request.resource.data.status == 'approved';\n      allow delete: if false;\n\n      // The actual marks: readable by the evaluator (it's their own input) and HR/Director (monitoring and\n      // official score calculation, see results.js::cohScoreFor) — never by the evaluatee. Immutable once\n      // written; a correction is a resubmit of the whole evaluation (both documents), not a patch here.\n      // Draft 0.32: every check on the parent is null-safe. get() on a parent that doesn't exist yet errors (= deny),\n      // which blocked every role without a separate way in (only Director, HR and Finance could evaluate).\n      match /private/scores {\n        // resource == null: the \"have I rated this colleague yet\" probe returns not-found instead of denied.\n        allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff())\n          || isDirector() || isHR() || can('performance.edit')\n          || (exists(evalDoc()) && get(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid);\n        // The parent and the scores are written in the same batch, so check the parent as it will be after the write.\n        allow create: if anyStaff()\n          && existsAfter(evalDoc())\n          && getAfter(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.ratings is list && request.resource.data.averageRating is number;\n        allow update: if anyStaff()\n          && exists(evalDoc())\n          && get(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid\n          // Draft 0.34: while 'submitted' the evaluator may change anything; once 'approved' only by ADDING answers\n          // (new questions), and the evaluation must go back to 'submitted' in the same write for re-review.\n          && (get(evalDoc()).data.status == 'submitted'\n            || (get(evalDoc()).data.status == 'approved'\n                && getAfter(evalDoc()).data.status == 'submitted'\n                && request.resource.data.ratings.size() > resource.data.ratings.size()))\n          && request.resource.data.ratings is list && request.resource.data.averageRating is number;\n        allow delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // KPI assignments: HR/Director create and edit; the employee and HR/Director read.\n    // (resource == null && anyStaff()) lets a getDoc() that's just probing \"does this exist yet\" return\n    // exists:false instead of permission-denied — without it, resource.data errors on a missing document and\n    // the whole rule denies, which is what was breaking the KPI page for a brand-new, never-submitted task.\n    match /kpiAssignments/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create, update: if isDirector();\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // KPI submissions: the employee submits their own self-assessment (status 'submitted', no final rating set\n    // yet); only HR/Director can set finalApprovedRating / reviewerId, and only by changing review fields.\n    // Draft 0.31: Director can also reopen done KPIs and send back for discussion.\n    match /kpiSubmissions/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      // The employee submits or resubmits their own self-assessment, but never once it's already been\n      // done (matches the KPI.vue UI, which hides the submit form at that point) — otherwise\n      // an employee could write status back to 'submitted' with nulled-out review fields and erase a\n      // reviewer's decision.\n      allow create, update: if (resource == null || (resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && resource.data.status != 'done'))\n        && request.resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && request.resource.data.get('finalApprovedRating', null) == null\n        && request.resource.data.get('reviewerId', null) == null;\n      // Director review and rating: provide rating/comments or approve/send back.\n      allow update: if isDirector()\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'revisedRating', 'finalApprovedRating', 'reviewerId', 'reviewerComments', 'reviewReason',\n          'directorRating', 'directorComments', 'directorId', 'ratedAt', 'discussionStatus', 'reviewedAt', 'history']);\n      // Director can reopen a done KPI and send it back for discussion (allows re-rating after approval).\n      allow update: if isDirector()\n        && resource.data.status == 'done'\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'discussionRequested'\n        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'directorRating', 'directorComments', 'directorId', 'ratedAt', 'discussionStatus', 'history']);\n      // The employee's own discussion-status flip, set alongside their replies.\n      allow update: if resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && changed().hasOnly(['discussionStatus']);\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // KPI conversation threads: complete discussion history for each KPI.\n    // Only the assigned employee and director can access.\n    // Draft 0.32: (resource == null && anyStaff()) so the chat's \"is there a thread yet\" probe isn't denied.\n    match /kpiConversations/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.assignmentId is string\n        && request.resource.data.employeeId is string && request.resource.data.directorId is string\n        && request.resource.data.messages is list && request.resource.data.status == 'active';\n      allow update: if (isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid)\n        && request.resource.data.messages is list;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // KPI discussion threads (deprecated): kept for backwards compatibility.\n    match /kpiDiscussions/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.submissionId is string && request.resource.data.employeeId is string\n        && request.resource.data.directorId is string && request.resource.data.thread is list && request.resource.data.status == 'active';\n      allow update: if (isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid) && request.resource.data.thread is list;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Discussion requests: the employee who raised it, and HR/Director, read and resolve.\n    match /performanceDiscussions/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create: if request.resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status == 'requested';\n      allow update: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit');\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // TMS performance snapshots: only HR/Director sync and approve (server-side TMS credentials never touch the\n    // frontend — this just writes the result). The employee reads their own; isFinal is never flipped back to false.\n    match /performanceTmsSnapshots/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create, update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit')) && (resource == null || resource.data.get('isFinal', false) != true);\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Final combined results, and the Stage 2 revision trail. Nobody — Director included — can write once\n    // approvalStatus is 'finalized', EXCEPT the one deliberate correction path: Director, going straight from\n    // 'finalized' to 'pendingApproval', bumping revisionNumber by exactly 1 and recording who/why. The app\n    // always writes a revisions/{rev} snapshot of the pre-correction values (results.js::requestCorrection)\n    // before this write, so a correction is never silently applied over the original finalized numbers.\n    match /performanceResults/{id} {\n      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n      allow create, update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit'))\n        && (resource == null || resource.data.get('approvalStatus', 'draft') != 'finalized');\n      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.get('approvalStatus', 'draft') == 'finalized'\n        && request.resource.data.approvalStatus == 'pendingApproval'\n        && request.resource.data.revisionNumber == resource.data.get('revisionNumber', 1) + 1\n        && request.resource.data.get('revisionReason', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('revisionReason', '').size() > 0\n        && request.resource.data.get('correctedBy', '') == request.auth.uid;\n      allow delete: if false;\n\n      // One immutable snapshot per revision, written right before the correction above.\n      match /revisions/{rev} {\n        allow read: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || get(/databases/$(database)/documents/performanceResults/$(id)).data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;\n        allow create: if isDirector();\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // ================= Agreements (Draft 0.14, 0.15) =================\n    function agreementAdmin() { return can('agreementSetup.view'); }\n\n    // Form fields, formulas and column-only fields. Archived, never deleted.\n    match /agreementForms/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.fields is list\n        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.fields is list && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Uploaded agreement PDFs (the file itself is in Drive), their versions and where each field prints.\n    match /agreementTemplates/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.mappings is list\n        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.mappings is list\n        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // One record per filled-in form. Everyone reads and writes; the form and the creator never change. Archived, never deleted.\n    match /agreementRecords/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.values is map\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['draft', 'submitted', 'completed', 'archived'] && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.values is map\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['draft', 'submitted', 'completed', 'archived']\n        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Master files: Word / Google Docs kept in Drive (\"Master File (DO NOT EDIT)\"). Only the record of them is here.\n    match /agreementMasters/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.docId is string && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.docId is string && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Fill-in links for outside people; the link name is the document id (/f/{slug}). Passwords are stored only as\n    // salt + SHA-256. \"Anyone\" links need Agreement Setup; any staff member may make a personal link for one record.\n    // Turned off or deleted (records already sent in stay). The Apps Script records submissions (it writes as the company account).\n    match /agreementLinks/{slug} {\n      function linkOk() {\n        return slug.matches('[a-z0-9-]{3,60}') && request.resource.data.slug == slug\n          && request.resource.data.kind in ['open', 'personal'] && request.resource.data.formId is string\n          && request.resource.data.get('passHash', '') is string;\n      }\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && linkOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && (agreementAdmin() || (request.resource.data.kind == 'personal' && request.resource.data.recordId is string));\n      allow update: if anyStaff() && linkOk() && request.resource.data.kind == resource.data.kind\n        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy\n        && (agreementAdmin() || resource.data.kind == 'personal');\n      // Agreement Setup deletes any link; other staff only the personal links they made.\n      allow delete: if anyStaff() && (agreementAdmin() || (resource.data.kind == 'personal' && resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid));\n    }\n\n    // Saved table layouts (columns, widths, filters). Shared by everyone.\n    match /agreementViews/{id} {\n      allow read, delete: if anyStaff();\n      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.view is map;\n    }\n\n    // History of generated PDFs. Written once by the person who made it.\n    match /generatedAgreements/{id} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.recordId is string\n        && request.resource.data.fileId is string;\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ================= Booking numbers (Booking Form, Create booking and the Willow Booking Details bulk upload) =================\n    // One counter per property prefix gives the next booking no. (DM-014). The Reservation Lodgment form is gone; offline bookings are the one booking record.\n    function lodgeStaff() { return finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view'); }\n    match /lodgmentCounters/{prefix} {\n      allow read: if lodgeStaff();\n      allow create, update: if lodgeStaff() && request.resource.data.next is int;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ================= Salary advances (Draft 0.42, 5 Nov 2026) =================\n    // Data shape and flow: src/pages/HR/advances.js.\n    function hrPath(uid)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/staffHR/$(uid); }\n    function limitPath(uid) { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advanceLimits/$(uid); }\n    function advPath(id)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advances/$(id); }\n    // HR and Directors keep the details; HR can't change their own (a Director does).\n    function hrDetailsEditor(uid) { return isDirector() || (isHR() && uid != request.auth.uid); }\n\n    // IC, position and monthly salary. Never readable by the staff member.\n    match /staffHR/{uid} {\n      allow read: if hrOrDir();\n      allow create, update: if hrDetailsEditor(uid)\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['ic', 'position', 'salary', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'updatedByName'])\n        && request.resource.data.ic is string && request.resource.data.position is string\n        && request.resource.data.salary is number && request.resource.data.salary >= 0\n        && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && getAfter(limitPath(uid)).data.limit == request.resource.data.salary * 0.5;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n    // The advance limit (50% of the salary): the only part the person reads.\n    match /advanceLimits/{uid} {\n      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || hrOrDir());\n      allow create, update: if hrDetailsEditor(uid)\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['limit', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.limit == getAfter(hrPath(uid)).data.salary * 0.5;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    match /advances/{id} {\n      function grows()     { return request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == resource.data.history.size() + 1; }\n      function from(a, b)  { return resource.data.status == a && request.resource.data.status == b; }\n      function onlyKeys(k) { return changed().hasOnly(['status', 'history', 'updatedAt'].concat(k)); }\n      // HR moves a request on, never their own.\n      function mover()     { return isHR() && resource.data.uid != request.auth.uid; }\n      function limitOfOwner() { return get(hrPath(resource.data.uid)).data.salary * 0.5; }\n      function sub(name, d)   { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advances/$(id)/$(name)/$(d); }\n      function mine()         { return signedIn() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid; }\n\n      allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid);\n      // Staff: their own request, Submitted, within 50% of the salary HR entered (no salary = refused). Not interns.\n      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid\n        && get(myRecord()).data.get('intern', false) != true\n        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'uid', 'name', 'amount', 'reason', 'neededBy', 'status', 'history', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'\n        && request.resource.data.ref is string && request.resource.data.name is string\n        && request.resource.data.amount is number && request.resource.data.amount > 0\n        && exists(hrPath(request.auth.uid))\n        && request.resource.data.amount <= get(hrPath(request.auth.uid)).data.salary * 0.5\n        && request.resource.data.reason is string && request.resource.data.reason.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.reason.size() <= 1000\n        && (!('neededBy' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.neededBy is string)\n        && request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == 1;\n      // HR: make the form for a staff member (byHR), straight at Reviewed; form/main and signatureUses in the same save.\n      allow create: if isHR() && request.resource.data.uid != request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.byHR == true\n        && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.resource.data.uid)).data.get('intern', false) != true\n        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'uid', 'name', 'amount', 'reason', 'description', 'status', 'byHR', 'approvedAmount', 'reviewedAt',\n          'reviewedBy', 'reviewedByName', 'reviewedDate', 'chloeTold', 'history', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.status == 'reviewed'\n        && request.resource.data.ref is string && request.resource.data.name is string\n        && request.resource.data.amount is number && request.resource.data.amount > 0\n        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount == request.resource.data.amount\n        && exists(hrPath(request.resource.data.uid))\n        && request.resource.data.amount <= get(hrPath(request.resource.data.uid)).data.salary * 0.5\n        && request.resource.data.reason is string && request.resource.data.reason.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.reason.size() <= 1000\n        && (!('description' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.description is string && request.resource.data.description.size() <= 1000))\n        && request.resource.data.reviewedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.chloeTold.by == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == 1\n        && existsAfter(sub('form', 'main'))\n        && existsAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatureUses/$(id));\n      // Staff: withdraw while Submitted.\n      allow update: if mine() && from('submitted', 'withdrawn')\n        && onlyKeys(['withdrawnAt']) && grows();\n      // HR: reject with a reason, at Submitted or Signed.\n      allow update: if mover() && (from('submitted', 'rejected') || from('signed', 'rejected')) && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['rejectReason', 'rejectedAt', 'rejectedBy', 'rejectedByName'])\n        && request.resource.data.rejectReason is string && request.resource.data.rejectReason.size() > 0\n        && request.resource.data.rejectedBy == request.auth.uid;\n      // HR: review (within the limit, Director told; form and signature-use line written in the same batch).\n      allow update: if mover() && from('submitted', 'reviewed') && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['approvedAmount', 'reviewedAt', 'reviewedBy', 'reviewedByName', 'reviewedDate', 'chloeTold'])\n        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount is number && request.resource.data.approvedAmount > 0\n        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount <= limitOfOwner()\n        && request.resource.data.reviewedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.chloeTold.by == request.auth.uid\n        && existsAfter(sub('form', 'main'))\n        && existsAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatureUses/$(id));\n      // Staff: sign (drawn on screen or a photo of the signed paper form, saved in signed/main in the same batch).\n      allow update: if mine() && from('reviewed', 'signed') && grows()\n        && resource.data.get('byHR', false) != true\n        && onlyKeys(['signMethod', 'signedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.signMethod in ['drawn', 'upload']\n        && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'main'));\n      // HR: signed outside the PMS; the fully signed document (signed/copy) is required.\n      allow update: if mover() && from('reviewed', 'signed') && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['signMethod', 'signedAt', 'signedCopyAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.signMethod == 'outside'\n        && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'main')) && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'copy'));\n      // HR: add or replace the fully signed document later (status unchanged).\n      allow update: if mover() && resource.data.status in ['signed', 'approved', 'paid']\n        && request.resource.data.status == resource.data.status && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['signedCopyAt']) && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'copy'));\n      // HR: approve (pending payment), then paid with type, date and screenshot.\n      allow update: if mover() && from('signed', 'approved') && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['approvedAt', 'approvedBy', 'approvedByName'])\n        && request.resource.data.approvedBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow update: if mover() && from('approved', 'paid') && grows()\n        && onlyKeys(['paidDate', 'paymentType', 'paidAt', 'paidBy', 'paidByName'])\n        && request.resource.data.paidDate is string && request.resource.data.paidBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.paymentType in ['tng', 'bank']\n        && existsAfter(sub('payment', 'main'));\n      allow delete: if false;\n\n      // The form as reviewed (IC, salary, Director's signature): the staff member, HR and Directors. Written once, at review.\n      match /form/{doc} {\n        allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid);\n        allow create: if isHR() && doc == 'main'\n          && ((!exists(advPath(id)) && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.byHR == true)\n            || get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'submitted')\n          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid\n          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed'\n          && request.resource.data.uid == getAfter(advPath(id)).data.uid\n          && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.signature == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatures/director).data.image;\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      // How it was signed (main) and the fully signed document (copy): the staff member, HR and Directors read.\n      // main: the staff member when signing (drawn / upload), or HR marking it signed outside. Written once.\n      // copy: HR only, required with 'outside', can be added or replaced while signed, approved or paid.\n      match /signed/{doc} {\n        function isImage() { return request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000; }\n        allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid);\n        allow create: if doc == 'main' && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid\n          && get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed' && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'signed'\n          && ((get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.method in ['drawn', 'upload'] && isImage())\n            || (isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.method == 'outside'));\n        allow create, update: if doc == 'copy' && isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid && isImage()\n          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status in ['signed', 'approved', 'paid'];\n        allow delete: if false;\n      }\n      // Payment screenshot: HR writes it with Paid; HR and Directors read (for the record, not the staff member).\n      match /payment/{doc} {\n        allow read: if hrOrDir();\n        allow create: if isHR() && doc == 'main' && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000\n          && get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'approved' && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'paid';\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n      // HR's own notes. HR writes; HR and Directors read (HR never on their own request).\n      match /notes/{noteId} {\n        allow read: if isDirector() || (isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid);\n        allow create: if isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['text', 'byName', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])\n          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid\n          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 1000;\n        allow update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // The Director's saved signature (default Miss Chloe), put on approved forms. HR uploads it for her; Directors may too.\n    match /signatures/{id} {\n      allow read: if hrOrDir();\n      allow create, update: if hrOrDir() && id == 'director'\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['signerName', 'image', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'updatedByName'])\n        && request.resource.data.signerName is string && request.resource.data.signerName.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.signerName.size() <= 100\n        && request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000\n        && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n    // One line per form that carries the signature (id = the advance). Written with the approval, never changed.\n    match /signatureUses/{id} {\n      allow read: if hrOrDir();\n      allow create: if isHR()\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['advanceId', 'ref', 'staffName', 'signerName', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'at'])\n        && request.resource.data.advanceId == id && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid\n        && ((!exists(advPath(id)) && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.byHR == true) || get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'submitted')\n        && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed';\n      allow update, delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // ---------------- Staff Attendance (Draft 0.49) ----------------\n    function attCfgPath() { return /databases/$(database)/documents/config/attendance; }\n    // Office settings. Until HR or a Director saves them, the defaults agreed on 11 Nov 2026 (Micasa Shoppes, 250 m, late after 9:10).\n    function attCfg() {\n      return exists(attCfgPath()) ? get(attCfgPath()).data\n        : {'lat': 3.156812, 'lng': 101.722188, 'radiusM': 250, 'cosLat': 0.998483, 'lateAfterMin': 550, 'workDays': [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],\n           'allowOffsite': true};\n    }\n    // Draft 0.54: clocking in / out away from the office is allowed (saved as Off-site, InArea false) unless HR turns it off.\n    // Draft 0.61: Normal (InArea true) means inside the main office (i == -1) or inside places[i]; the server does the\n    // distance sum for the place the phone names, so nobody can mark themselves Normal or name a place they aren't at.\n    // name: 'WIDEBED' or the place's name when Normal, the looked-up address when Off-site (null = an older app).\n    function attPlaces() { return attCfg().get('places', []); }\n    function attSpot(i) { return i == -1 ? attCfg() : attPlaces()[i]; }\n    function attPlaceOk(lat, lng, inArea, i, name) {\n      return lat is number && lng is number && inArea is bool\n        && (inArea\n            ? (i is int && i >= -1 && i < attPlaces().size() && attNear(lat, lng, attSpot(i))\n                && (name == null || name == (i == -1 ? 'WIDEBED' : attSpot(i).name)))\n            : (attCfg().get('allowOffsite', true) == true && (name == null || (name is string && name.size() <= 200))));\n    }\n    function attPad(n) { return n < 10 ? '0' + string(n) : string(n); }\n    // The server's time in Malaysia (UTC+8, no daylight saving).\n    function myNow() { return request.time + duration.value(8, 'h'); }\n    function attToday() { let t = myNow(); return string(t.year()) + '-' + attPad(t.month()) + '-' + attPad(t.day()); }\n    // Inside a place's circle (the main office or one of places), from the phone's reported position\n    // (metres, flat-earth sum: exact enough at these sizes).\n    function attNear(lat, lng, p) {\n      let dy = (lat - p.lat) * 111320;\n      let dx = (lng - p.lng) * 111320 * p.cosLat;\n      return dy * dy + dx * dx <= p.radiusM * p.radiusM;\n    }\n    // Draft 0.59: a holiday counts for you unless HR left you out of it (exceptUids).\n    function attHolidayForMe(date) {\n      let p = /databases/$(database)/documents/attendanceHolidays/$(date);\n      return exists(p) && !(request.auth.uid in get(p).data.get('exceptUids', []));\n    }\n    function attWorkDay(date) {\n      return myNow().dayOfWeek() in attCfg().workDays && !attHolidayForMe(date);\n    }\n    function attLate(date) {\n      let t = myNow();\n      return attWorkDay(date) && t.hours() * 60 + t.minutes() > attCfg().lateAfterMin;\n    }\n    // Draft 0.52: the session before n (today, this person) exists and is clocked out.\n    function attPrevId(n) {\n      return n == 2 ? request.auth.uid + '_' + attToday() : request.auth.uid + '_' + attToday() + '_s' + string(n - 1);\n    }\n    function attPrevClosed(n) {\n      let p = /databases/$(database)/documents/attendance/$(attPrevId(n));\n      return exists(p) && ('clockOut' in get(p).data);\n    }\n\n    match /attendance/{id} {\n      // Your own records (a list query must filter uid == you). resource == null: \"has today's record been made yet?\"\n      allow read: if hrOrDir() || (anyStaff() && (resource == null || resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid));\n      // Clock in (Draft 0.52: several per day). Session 1 is {uid}_{day} and decides late / off day; going out and coming back\n      // makes session 2, 3… ({uid}_{day}_s2 …, at most 10), allowed only once the one before is clocked out. Never late.\n      allow create: if anyStaff()\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['uid', 'name', 'department', 'role', 'date', 'session', 'clockIn', 'clockInLat',\n             'clockInLng', 'clockInAccuracy', 'clockInDistance', 'clockInInArea', 'clockInMocked', 'late', 'lateReason', 'offDay',\n             'status', 'platform', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt', 'clockInPlace', 'clockInPlaceIdx'])\n        && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.date == attToday()\n        && request.resource.data.clockIn == request.time\n        && request.resource.data.createdAt == request.time\n        && request.resource.data.updatedAt == request.time\n        && request.resource.data.clockInMocked == false\n        && attPlaceOk(request.resource.data.clockInLat, request.resource.data.clockInLng, request.resource.data.clockInInArea,\n             request.resource.data.get('clockInPlaceIdx', -1), request.resource.data.get('clockInPlace', null))\n        && request.resource.data.offDay == !attWorkDay(attToday())\n        && request.resource.data.late is bool\n        && ((\n              !('session' in request.resource.data)\n              && id == request.auth.uid + '_' + attToday()\n              && (!attLate(attToday()) || request.resource.data.late == true)\n              && (request.resource.data.late == false\n                  || (request.resource.data.lateReason is string && request.resource.data.lateReason.size() >= 3\n                      && request.resource.data.lateReason.size() <= 300))\n              && request.resource.data.status == (request.resource.data.offDay ? 'offDay' : (request.resource.data.late ? 'late' : 'present'))\n            ) || (\n              request.resource.data.session is int\n              && request.resource.data.session >= 2 && request.resource.data.session <= 10\n              && id == request.auth.uid + '_' + attToday() + '_s' + string(request.resource.data.session)\n              && attPrevClosed(request.resource.data.session)\n              && request.resource.data.late == false\n              && !('lateReason' in request.resource.data)\n              && request.resource.data.status == (request.resource.data.offDay ? 'offDay' : 'present')\n            ));\n      // Clock out: once, the same Malaysia day, with the server's time (in the area, or Off-site if allowed: Draft 0.54).\n      // Then (second save) workedMinutes, which must equal clockOut - clockIn from the two server times (rounded down, 1 min slack).\n      allow update: if anyStaff()\n        && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid\n        && ((\n              resource.data.date == attToday()\n              && !('clockOut' in resource.data)\n              && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['clockOut', 'clockOutLat', 'clockOutLng',\n                   'clockOutAccuracy', 'clockOutDistance', 'clockOutInArea', 'clockOutMocked', 'updatedAt', 'clockOutPlace', 'clockOutPlaceIdx'])\n              && request.resource.data.clockOut == request.time\n              && request.resource.data.updatedAt == request.time\n              && request.resource.data.clockOutMocked == false\n              && attPlaceOk(request.resource.data.clockOutLat, request.resource.data.clockOutLng, request.resource.data.clockOutInArea,\n                   request.resource.data.get('clockOutPlaceIdx', -1), request.resource.data.get('clockOutPlace', null))\n            ) || (\n              'clockOut' in resource.data\n              && !('workedMinutes' in resource.data)\n              && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['workedMinutes'])\n              && request.resource.data.workedMinutes is int\n              && request.resource.data.workedMinutes >= (resource.data.clockOut.toMillis() - resource.data.clockIn.toMillis()) / 60000 - 1\n              && request.resource.data.workedMinutes <= (resource.data.clockOut.toMillis() - resource.data.clockIn.toMillis()) / 60000 + 1\n            ));\n      // Draft 0.51: HR / Director corrections (PMS Attendance page). Never their own record; the person and the date stay.\n      allow create, update: if hrOrDir()\n        && request.resource.data.uid is string && request.resource.data.uid != request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.date is string && request.resource.data.date.matches('^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$')\n        && (id == request.resource.data.uid + '_' + request.resource.data.date\n            || id == request.resource.data.uid + '_' + request.resource.data.date + '_s' + string(request.resource.data.get('session', 0)))\n        && (resource == null || (resource.data.uid == request.resource.data.uid && resource.data.date == request.resource.data.date))\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['uid', 'name', 'department', 'role', 'date', 'session', 'clockIn', 'clockInLat', 'clockInLng',\n             'clockInAccuracy', 'clockInDistance', 'clockInInArea', 'clockInMocked', 'late', 'lateReason', 'offDay', 'status',\n             'platform', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt', 'clockOut', 'clockOutLat', 'clockOutLng', 'clockOutAccuracy', 'clockOutDistance',\n             'clockOutInArea', 'clockOutMocked', 'workedMinutes', 'editedBy', 'editedByName', 'editedAt', 'editNote',\n             'clockInPlace', 'clockInPlaceIdx', 'clockOutPlace', 'clockOutPlaceIdx'])\n        && request.resource.data.clockIn is timestamp\n        && (!('clockOut' in request.resource.data)\n            || (request.resource.data.clockOut is timestamp && request.resource.data.clockOut > request.resource.data.clockIn))\n        && (!('workedMinutes' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.workedMinutes is int)\n        && request.resource.data.status in ['present', 'late', 'offDay']\n        && request.resource.data.editedBy == request.auth.uid\n        && request.resource.data.editedAt == request.time\n        && request.resource.data.editNote is string && request.resource.data.editNote.size() >= 3 && request.resource.data.editNote.size() <= 300;\n      allow delete: if false;\n    }\n\n    // Public holidays, kept by HR on the PMS Attendance page. id = YYYY-MM-DD.\n    match /attendanceHolidays/{date} {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      // Draft 0.59: exceptUids = staff left out of this holiday (empty or missing = everyone).\n      allow create, update: if hrOrDir() && date.matches('^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$')\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['name', 'exceptUids', 'addedBy', 'addedAt', 'updatedBy', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() <= 80\n        && request.resource.data.get('exceptUids', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('exceptUids', []).size() <= 300;\n      allow delete: if hrOrDir() && date.matches('^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$');\n    }\n\n    // Office location, radius and late time for attendance. Draft 0.61: places = the other locations (properties), up to 30.\n    match /config/attendance {\n      allow read: if anyStaff();\n      allow write: if hrOrDir()\n        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['officeName', 'address', 'lat', 'lng', 'radiusM', 'cosLat', 'workStartMin',\n             'workEndMin', 'lateAfterMin', 'workDays', 'allowOffsite', 'places', 'updatedBy', 'updatedAt'])\n        && request.resource.data.get('places', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('places', []).size() <= 30\n        && request.resource.data.get('allowOffsite', true) is bool\n        && request.resource.data.lat is number && request.resource.data.lng is number\n        && request.resource.data.radiusM is number && request.resource.data.radiusM >= 50 && request.resource.data.radiusM <= 2000\n        && request.resource.data.cosLat is number && request.resource.data.lateAfterMin is int && request.resource.data.workDays is list;\n    }\n\n  }\n}\n","name":"firebase/firestore.rules"}]},"createTime":"2026-11-12T07:31:32.835471Z","metadata":{"services":["cloud.firestore"]}}
